# fail-error-map: pins the whole map a Host `Fail` raises, which a case that
# catches the error never prints. Nothing catches it, so the Run ends
# `errored` and its `run` record writes the map, with its keys in chapter 6's
# order:
#
# - `code` and `message`, as the Host gave them. A Host-made `message` is
#   kept, since only a Core-raised one's wording is outside parity.
# - The `Data` entries, in the order the Host gave them (`due`, then `left`),
#   not the order the Operation declares them.
# - `capability`, `operation` and `at`, which the Core adds. `at` is the
#   `ask … and wait` (shop:3, pos 5:3).
#
# shop has no `on error`, so the `error` message is dropped, with no record.
# Fuel, allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load shop

> deliver d1 to=shop message=check args=["A1"]
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
call shop/r1.c1 op=stock.check args=["A1"]
seg shop/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=check clause=1 fuel=103 alloc=0 state=0 end=ask-wait
pumped state=idle fuel=103 next=2026-09-30T10:00:30Z

> fail shop/r1.c1 error={code: "out of stock", message: "None left", due: "Friday", left: 0}
> pump clock=2026-09-30T10:00:01Z
raise shop/r1 code="out of stock" at=shop:3 pos=5:3
seg shop/r1 resume fuel=6 alloc=160 state=0 end=error
run shop/r1 outcome=errored delivery=d1 handler=check error={code: "out of stock", message: "None left", due: "Friday", left: 0, capability: "stock", operation: "check", at: {unit: "shop", handler: "check", line: 5, column: 3}} fuel=109 alloc=160
pumped state=idle fuel=6

> vars
vars shop
